{
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "title",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "# filecache / vidcache — Two-Phase Client Upload\n`client.upload_init()` + `client.upload_stream()` (manual) **or** `client.ingest_from_url()` (combined)\nBytes stream from client → service. URL dedup check skips upload if already cached.",
      "x": 0,
      "y": -240,
      "width": 640,
      "height": 110
    },
    {
      "id": "start",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "**START**\nScraper wants to upload a file/video to the cache",
      "x": 0,
      "y": -70,
      "width": 640,
      "height": 70,
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "s1",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "**[Scraper]** — choose one of two entry points:\n• `client.upload_init(url, bucket, filename=…)` then `client.upload_stream(upload_id, stream)`\n• `client.ingest_from_url(url, bucket, filename=…)` — combines both phases automatically",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 60,
      "width": 640,
      "height": 100
    },
    {
      "id": "phase1-group",
      "type": "group",
      "label": "Phase 1 — Init & Dedup Check",
      "x": -20,
      "y": 200,
      "width": 680,
      "height": 290
    },
    {
      "id": "s2",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "**[StreamingCacheClient]**\n`POST /upload/init` with JSON:\n`{ url, bucket, filename, [prefix, meta, content_hash] }`",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 240,
      "width": 640,
      "height": 90
    },
    {
      "id": "s3",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "**[service → PostgreSQL]**\nChecks if URL (and optional content_hash) is already stored in this bucket",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 370,
      "width": 640,
      "height": 80
    },
    {
      "id": "decision",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "URL already cached?",
      "x": 170,
      "y": 530,
      "width": 300,
      "height": 60,
      "color": "3"
    },
    {
      "id": "dedup-hit",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "**YES — dedup hit**\nReturns `{ status: \"cached\" | \"fresh\", hash, file_path }`\nUpload skipped entirely",
      "x": -260,
      "y": 650,
      "width": 340,
      "height": 90,
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "dedup-miss",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "**NO — not cached**\nReturns `{ status: \"pending\", upload_id }`",
      "x": 240,
      "y": 650,
      "width": 340,
      "height": 70,
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "phase2-group",
      "type": "group",
      "label": "Phase 2 — Stream Upload",
      "x": -20,
      "y": 770,
      "width": 680,
      "height": 320
    },
    {
      "id": "s4",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "**[Scraper / ingest_from_url]** — choose one:\n• Manual: Scraper reads local bytes and calls `client.upload_stream(upload_id, file_object)`\n• ingest_from_url: Client downloads source URL on-the-fly and pipes chunks directly — nothing written to disk locally",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 810,
      "width": 640,
      "height": 100
    },
    {
      "id": "s5",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "**[StreamingCacheClient]**\n`POST /upload/{upload_id}` with chunked binary body\n`Content-Type: application/octet-stream`",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 950,
      "width": 640,
      "height": 90
    },
    {
      "id": "s6",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "**[service]**\nReceives chunks, writes to local file storage\nComputes blake3 content hash of received bytes",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 1090,
      "width": 640,
      "height": 80
    },
    {
      "id": "s7",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "**[service → PostgreSQL]**\nInserts cache entry: `url, hash, bucket, file_path, size_bytes, stored_at, [filename, prefix, meta]`",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 1220,
      "width": 640,
      "height": 80
    },
    {
      "id": "s8",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "**[service]**\nReturns `{ status: \"stored\", hash, file_path, size_bytes }`",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 1350,
      "width": 640,
      "height": 70
    },
    {
      "id": "merge",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "**[StreamingCacheClient]**\nReturns result dict to caller",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 1470,
      "width": 640,
      "height": 70
    },
    {
      "id": "end",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "**END**\nCaller receives `{ status, hash, file_path, [size_bytes] }`",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 1590,
      "width": 640,
      "height": 70,
      "color": "4"
    }
  ],
  "edges": [
